From 77b9df7fbe21a8e7a9ed4697e8af16e0b5d53f27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:03:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 104/118] scripting: thisLayer and thisObject are the script
 running now

WE defines both as accessors on the global (scenescript64.dll: getters 0x1810d5fd0 and
0x1810d60d0, set on the global template at 0x1810d89d3 / 0x1810d8a29) that return the object of
the last entry of the engine's running-script deque (engine +0x4b0), undefined when none. Code a
script shares therefore sees its caller: 3163060610's clocks register an event listener (a class
from another object's script) that keeps `thisObject` and writes its text there; with LWE's
module-scope bindings it wrote to the other object and the clocks stayed "Loading...".

The engine now pushes [layer, object] around every entry into a script (a module's evaluation
and exports, a text layer's script, its hooks and events); a timer or a video-ended callback
runs with the script that set it (Inferred: WE's timers are not decoded).

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Preview compare result" (3163060610)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
